**Library**: A collection of functions/tools you call when needed. You control the flow. **Framework**: A structure that calls YOUR code (Inversion of Control). Framework dictates the architecture.

```javascript
// Library example (jQuery - you call it)
$(document).ready(function() {
    $('button').click(function() {
        $('.result').text('Clicked!');
    });
});

// Framework example (Angular - framework calls you)
// Angular component - framework controls lifecycle
@Component({
    selector: 'app-button',
    template: '<button (click)="onClick()">{{message}}</button>'
})
export class ButtonComponent {
    message = 'Click me';
    onClick() { this.message = 'Clicked!'; }
}
```

